From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:04:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Atmosphere: the real Moon, a night sky image, lunar and
 solar eclipses; compiler threads

For the GMod companion's sky (native loader repo, ADR 0032):

- Moon 0 can be drawn as the real Moon from DDS maps beside d3d9.dll
  (rtx.atmosphere.moonTextureEnable, moonAlbedoTexture, moonNormalTexture, moonTextureAlbedo,
  moonReliefStrength): a sphere in selenographic coordinates, north towards the ecliptic pole,
  lit by Lommel-Seeliger plus a little Lambert from a sun the phase option places on the real sun's
  side of the sky, with relief from the normal map and earthshine on the night side. The terminator
  follows the smooth sphere over about two pixels; the relief's cos i goes through a softplus.
- A night sky image can replace the procedural star field (rtx.atmosphere.starMapEnable): the
  star, galaxy and nebula layers of the Night Sky HD layout (starMapTexture, starMapGalaxyTexture,
  starMapNebulaTexture), each sampled through the analytic mapping of that mod's sky meshes in an
  equatorial frame turned by the star axis and starRotation (-LST), added in gamma space as Skyrim
  blends them, then decoded and scaled by starMapBrightness (0.12).
- Eclipses from the geometry (rtx.atmosphere.eclipseEnable and the eclipse* scales): Earth's umbra
  and penumbra shade moon 0 per pixel, and their disc average scales and reddens moon 0's colour for
  every moonlight path; while moon 0 nears the sun a sun disc sized from it is drawn on primary rays,
  with the chromosphere and a corona, and the covered fraction scales sunIlluminance (floor
  eclipseTotalityLight). Stars come out at totality. The disc and the Moon's silhouette take two
  pixels and the disc is capped at 16384, so the upscaler does not ring into black pixels.
- RtxAtmosphere loads the textures itself (AssetDataManager + updateImage, one upload per path),
  only in Numos sessions and only what is enabled; a 1x1 stand-in is bound otherwise. Bindings 216
  (a retired slot), 217-219 and 221 (collision audit in common_binding_indices.h). Their mips come
  from the traced pixel's angle with the materials' upscaler mip bias. AtmosphereArgs takes
  padAerial7/8 and grows by three 16-byte rows, all zeroed in normalizeForSkyLutCache.
- dxvk.numCompilerThreads below 0 means all hardware threads but that many (dxvk_state_cache.cpp).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
